{{Unobtainable}}
'''Maiko Cat''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that was introduced in [[Version 2.0 Update|Version 2.0]] and can be unlocked by special [[:Category:Serial Code Cats|serial code]] included in [[Nyanko Ecology Report]]. It is now unobtainable due to serial codes being removed as a feature in the mobile version. In [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], beating [[Egypt (Empire of Cats)|Egypt]] (京都府, <b>Kyoto</b> in the Japanese Version) 10 times with [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]] in the lineup will grant you access to the unit. 

{{Cat Info
|ID = 45
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Maiko Cat
|name2 = Geisha Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Geisha Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Very similar to [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]] in terms of usage. Cheap and expendable, it can be summoned en masse to take hits in place of other, important units. This meatshield role is quite valuable, if not for the wide selection of cats able to perform this role without relevant differences in quality. Maiko Cat, however, can be used in 4-crown stages, where there is considerably less competition. This is her only real use.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Due to the low stats, this form is not recommended as it is considerably worse than any possible alternative in about every way, making her a waste of money when summoned. Could still be of use in early-mid [[Empire of Cats]], but, after that, it is best to revert this cat to her Normal Form and only use that.

{{Job|EvolvedClass = Midranger|Classification = Meatshield|TrueClass=|UltraClass=}}

